{"type":"text","timestamp":1770334552993,"sessionID":"ses_3cfd761e5ffeJHdwuexgA0w6qm","part":{"id":"prt_c30297c2b001ptxWXIlbdeZdLB","sessionID":"ses_3cfd761e5ffeJHdwuexgA0w6qm","messageID":"msg_c302972af0018N6pFn6ZaQdImd","type":"text","text":"I have created a server component `UserPreferences` that reads the `theme` cookie and the `Accept-Language` header using Next.js `cookies()` and `headers()` APIs.\n\nHere is the plan I executed:\n1.  Created `app/components/UserPreferences.tsx` which implements the requested logic.\n2.  Updated `app/page.tsx` to render this component.\n3.  Verified the application builds successfully.\n\nYou can see the implementation below:\n\n`app/components/UserPreferences.tsx`:\n```tsx\nimport { cookies, headers } from 'next/headers';\n\nexport default async function UserPreferences() {\n  const cookieStore = await cookies();\n  const theme = cookieStore.get('theme')?.value || 'light';\n\n  const headersList = await headers();\n  const acceptLanguage = headersList.get('accept-language') || 'unknown';\n\n  return (\n    <div style={{ padding: '1rem', border: '1px solid #ccc', borderRadius: '4px', marginTop: '1rem' }}>\n      <h2>Preferences</h2>\n      <p><strong>Theme:</strong> {theme}</p>\n      <p><strong>Language:</strong> {acceptLanguage}</p>\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n```","time":{"start":1770334552992,"end":1770334552992}}}
